      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm trying to clean up some legacy data in our production DB and it's a bit of a mess. we have a lot of redundant info across different tables that's making queries slow and causing sync issues. what are some standard best practices or specific patterns i should look for to identify where we have redundant data that needs to be normalized?",
